--[[
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        PLUG-AND-PLAY SCRIPT TEMPLATE — Compkiller UI (v5)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Drop this file in, rename the Window/Config names, delete the
    example elements you don't need, and start wiring real features
    into the Section:Add___ callbacks below.

    Everything here mirrors the current library API documented in
    Ui/DocUpdated.lua and demonstrated in Ui/Example.lua, plus the
    exact UI Settings / Config wiring pattern already proven out in
    Owner/BaseTemplate.lua (Bishop Hub).

    New in this pass:
      • AddToggle now accepts a Toggles = { <ToggleConfig>, ... } list of
        nested sub-toggles that only show up while the parent is on — e.g.
        an "Auto Ability" toggle revealing the toggles that configure it.
        Opt-in (existing toggles are unaffected) — see "Sub-Toggles" in
        Test Lab below.
      • AddDropdown now accepts a Refresh = function(currentDefault) return
        newValues, newDefault end callback, called every time the dropdown
        is opened — for lists that change on their own (players in the
        server, active jobs, etc). Also new: :SetRefresh(fn) to attach/
        detach it later, and :Refresh() to pull an update on demand. Opt-in
        — see "Target Player (Live)" under Dropdowns in Test Lab below.
      • The right-click "configure keybind" panel (Hold/Toggle + key, on
        every toggle/slider) is now a proper popover context menu that
        spawns at the cursor — rounded, translucent, with a header, a
        pulsing "listening..." state while capturing a key, a Hold/Toggle
        segmented control, and a Clear Bind option. Purely visual — nothing
        to change, it just looks and feels better now.
      • New Dynamic Sound FX: subtle audio feedback for clicks (including
        tab switches — everything clickable routes through the same
        internal wrapper), toggles, and notifications via
        Compkiller:PlaySFX(name, volumeMul?). Ships with real default
        sounds and works out of the box; "Enable Sound Effects" and "SFX
        Volume" are auto-added to UI Settings → Controls. Swap in your own
        sounds any time with Compkiller:SetSFX(name, assetId) — see "Sound
        Effects" in Test Lab below.

    Everything above this line needs the opt-in bits wired if you want them
    (or nothing at all for the popover/SFX-settings pieces). Everything
    below was already true as of the previous pass and needs no wiring:
      • Ctrl+K (or the "Search" row at the bottom of the tab sidebar,
        below the tab list) opens a global fuzzy search over every
        tab/section/element name in the window (including inside
        DrawContainerTab sub-tabs and collapsed sections) and jumps
        straight to the specific element, blinking it a few times.
      • Any slider's value label can be clicked to type a number in
        directly instead of dragging.
      • AddButton takes an optional Confirm = true (see the
        "Confirm Delete" button in Test Lab) for a reusable double-
        click-to-confirm on risky actions, instead of hand-rolling
        the double-click timer per script.
      • AddParagraph content now wraps to multiple lines instead of
        getting clipped when it's long.
      • Dropdown rows highlight on hover, and single-select dropdowns
        now close themselves after you pick a value.
      • The Config tab's old standalone "Import" button is gone —
        pasting a config code into the name box and hitting Enter (or
        "Add Config") still imports it, same as before.
      • The window is now resizable — drag the small grip in the
        bottom-right corner (desktop only). Persists across the
        Insert/toggle keybind hiding and reshowing the window.
      • Notifier.new() now collapses an exact repeat (same Title AND
        Content) of a toast still on screen into a "×N" counter instead
        of stacking duplicates — useful if a loop ever fires the same
        notification every frame.
      • UI Settings → Custom Colors gained "Risky" and "Toggle (On State)"
        color pickers, and every swatch there now updates to match
        whichever built-in theme preset you pick from the Theme dropdown.
      • UI Settings → Saved Themes (new section): save/load/delete your
        own named color palettes independent of the config system — see
        Ui/DocUpdated.lua's DrawUISettings section for the full API.
      • Config tab: the ACTIVE/AUTO badges are now solid pill chips, rows
        have more breathing room, the icon-only buttons (copy/rename/
        duplicate/auto-load/delete) show their name on hover, and Delete
        uses the same Confirm primitive as AddButton (with a real ~2.5s
        countdown toast) instead of a one-off timer. Also fixed a bug:
        clicking Save on a config no longer marks it ACTIVE — Save just
        overwrites that file, ACTIVE only changes on Load.
      • Color pickers (AddColorPicker) got a real fix, not just a tweak:
        dragging the box/hue-strip/opacity-strip used to read mouse
        position in a coordinate space that didn't match the UI's own
        (IgnoreGuiInset), which is what made the picker feel like it was
        placing the dot somewhere other than the cursor. Dragging is now
        1:1 and accurate. The hex code under the picker is also editable
        now — type a color in directly instead of only dragging to it.
]]

